the soft hyphen, the first zero-width code point: 1 0 1
combining marks: 1 0 0 1
Hangul leading consonants (wide), vowels and trailing consonants (zero): 1 2 2 0 0 0 0 1
the zero-width space and joiner: 1 0 0 0 1
a combining mark that is also wide: 1 0 0 2
CJK unified ideographs: 2 2 2 2
Hangul syllables: 1 2 2 1
the byte order mark: 1 0 1
fullwidth forms: 1 2 2 1
regional indicators, one each: 1 1 1 2
emoji: 2 2 2 1
the CJK planes, their unassigned parts included: 1 2 2 1 1 2 2 1
the last code points: 0 1 0 0 1 1
a lone continuation byte: 1
an overlong form, two bad bytes: 2
a surrogate, three bad bytes: 3
a wide character cut short, two bad bytes: 2
a bad byte inside text: 5
a bad byte before a wide character: 3
all 256 bytes, 128 characters and 128 bad bytes: 256
